{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-exo-24-1","title":"Exodus 24:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":24,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":24,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Moses is called up into the mountain. 3 The people promise obedience. 4 Moses builds an altar, and twelve pillars. 6 He sprinkles the blood of the covenant. 9 The glory of God appears. 14 Aaron and Hur have the charge of the people. 15 Moses goes into the mountain, where he continues forty days and forty nights.</p>\n<p>Come up. 15; 3:5; 19:9,20,24; 20:21; 34:2 Nadab. 6:23; 28:1; Le 10:1,2; 1Ch 6:3 seventy. 9; 1:5; Nu 11:16,24,25; Eze 8:11; Lu 10:1,17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-24-2","title":"Exodus 24:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":24,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":24,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>13,15,18; 20:21; Nu 16:5; Jer 30:21; 49:19; Heb 9:24; 10:21,22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-24-3","title":"Exodus 24:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":24,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":24,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>all the judgments. 21:1-23:33; De 4:1,5,45; 5:1,31; 6:1; 11:1 All the words. 7; 19:8; De 5:27,28; Jos 24:22; Ga 3:19,20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-24-4","title":"Exodus 24:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":24,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":24,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>wrote. De 31:9; Jos 24:26 and builded. 20:24-26 twelve pillars. Ge 28:18,22; 31:45; Jos 24:27; Ga 2:9 according. 28:21; Le 24:5; Nu 17:2; Jos 4:2,3,8,9,20; 1Ki 11:30; Ezr 6:17 Lu 22:30; Re 21:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-24-5","title":"Exodus 24:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":24,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":24,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>young men. 19:22 burnt offerings. 18:12; Le 1:1-17 peace offerings. Le 3:1-17; 7:11-21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-24-6","title":"Exodus 24:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":24,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":24,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>the blood he. 8; 12:7,22; Col 1:20; Heb 9:18; 12:24; 1Pe 1:2,19 on the altar. 29:16,20; Le 1:5,11; 3:2,8; 4:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-24-7","title":"Exodus 24:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":24,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":24,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>the book. 4; Heb 9:18-23 read. De 31:11-13; Ac 13:15; Col 4:16; 1Th 5:27 All that. 3; Jer 7:23,24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-24-8","title":"Exodus 24:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":24,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":24,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>sprinkled. 6; Le 8:30; Isa 52:15; Eze 36:25; Heb 9:18-21 Behold. Zec 9:11; Mt 26:28; Mr 14:24; Lu 22:20; 1Co 11:25; Eph 1:7 Heb 9:20; 10:4,5; 13:20; 1Pe 1:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-24-10","title":"Exodus 24:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":24,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":24,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>saw. 10; 3:6; 33:20,23; Ge 32:30; Jud 13:21,22; 1Ki 22:19; Isa 6:1-5 Eze 1:28; Joh 1:18; 14:9; 1Ti 6:16; 1Jo 4:12 of a sapphire stone.The Hebrew {sappir,} is without doubt the sapphire; which is a most beautiful precious stone of a fine blue colour, second only to the diamond in lustre, hardness, and value. The ancient oriental sapphire is supposed to have been the same as the lapis lazuli. It glitters with golden spots; and is of an azure or sky-blue colour, but rarely intermixed with purple. The ruby and topaz are considered of the same genus.</p>\n<p>Eze 1:26,27; 10:1; Re 4:3; 21:19-23 in his clearness. So 6:10; Mt 17:2; Re 1:16; 21:11,18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-24-11","title":"Exodus 24:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":24,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":24,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>nobles. 1,9; Nu 21:18; Jud 5:13; 1Ki 21:8; 2Ch 23:20; Ne 2:16; Jer 14:3 laid not. 19:21; 33:20-23; Ge 32:24-32; De 4:33; Jud 13:22 they saw. 10; Ge 16:13 did eat. 18:12; Ge 18:18; 31:54; De 12:7; Ec 9:7; Lu 15:23,24; 1Co 10:16-18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-24-12","title":"Exodus 24:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":24,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":24,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>Come up. 2,15,18 tables. 31:18; 32:15,16; De 5:22; Ne 9:13; Jer 31:33; 2Co 3:3,7; Heb 9:4 that thou. De 4:14; Ezr 7:10; Mt 5:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-24-13","title":"Exodus 24:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":24,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":24,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>his minister. 17:9-14; 32:17; 33:11; Nu 11:28 went up. 2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-24-14","title":"Exodus 24:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":24,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":24,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>Tarry ye. 32:1; Ge 22:5; 1Sa 10:8; 13:8-13 Hur. 17:10,12 if any man. 18:25,26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-24-15","title":"Exodus 24:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":24,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":24,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>a cloud. 19:9,16; 2Ch 6:1; Mt 17:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-24-16","title":"Exodus 24:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":24,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":24,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>the glory. 17; 16:10; Le 9:23; Nu 14:10; 16:42; Eze 1:28; 2Co 4:6 seventh day. 19:11; 20:10; Re 1:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-24-17","title":"Exodus 24:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":24,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":24,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>like devouring fire. 3:2; 19:18; De 4:24,36; Eze 1:27; Na 1:6; Hab 3:4,5; Heb 12:18,29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-24-18","title":"Exodus 24:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":24,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":24,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>went into. 17; 9:29,33; 19:20; Pr 28:1 forty days. 34:28; De 9:9,18,25; 10:10; 1Ki 19:8; Mt 4:2; Mr 1:13; Lu 4:2</p>"}]}